# by the Omen alone, CR 720.3a), though Bot1 has the mana and Golos is there to target; on Bot1's own main phase it is
# (the positive control). It may target only a creature without flying, so Bot2's Ornithopter is refused, and its 5
# damage kills Golos, Tireless Pilgrim, a 3/5 (four would not). It costs the Omen's {1}{R}, paid by a Mountain and a Mox
# Ruby. As it resolves its controller shuffles it into its owner's library instead of putting it into the graveyard (CR
# 720.3d): Bot1's library grows by one (seven left after the turn-3 draw, eight after), and nothing of Bot1's is in the
# graveyard or exile. The creature was never cast, so no enters trigger gained Bot1 5 life.

